WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:19.564
knew the campers were doing something messy today.

2
00:00:20.564 --> 00:00:23.025
The picnic table was covered with garbage bags.

3
00:00:24.086 --> 00:00:24.566
And Mr.

4
00:00:24.606 --> 00:00:26.867
Dunn was wearing an apron and rubber gloves.

5
00:00:26.887 --> 00:00:29.608
"Great!" Izzie thought.

6
00:00:30.536 --> 00:00:31.636
Messy meant fun!

7
00:00:31.656 --> 00:00:36.238
"It looks like Laundry Day," Bobby said.

8
00:00:37.238 --> 00:00:40.039
He pointed to a bucket of water filled with T-shirts.

9
00:00:40.059 --> 00:00:42.179
"Nope," Mr.

10
00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:43.600
Dunn said with a smile.

11
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.740
"It's Tie-dyed T-shirt Day!"

12
00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:51.002
Mr. Dunn held up a blue and green T-shirt.

13
00:00:52.182 --> 00:00:56.883
It was tie-dyed and had the words "Kids Central Summer Camp" on it.

14
00:00:58.103 --> 00:00:59.864
"Awesome!" Izzie cried.

15
00:01:00.804 --> 00:01:01.765
"I want that shirt!

16
00:01:02.926 --> 00:01:04.927
I'm going to make one exactly like it."

17
00:01:06.428 --> 00:01:10.071
"Grab your aprons and a pair of gloves, campers," said Mr.

18
00:01:10.111 --> 00:01:14.494
Dunn. "You don't want the dye getting on your skin or clothes.

19
00:01:15.795 --> 00:01:17.636
Only on the shirt you're dying!"

20
00:01:18.436 --> 00:01:19.697
Mr. Dunn chuckled.

21
00:01:20.918 --> 00:01:23.420
"Start by choosing a T-shirt from the bucket."

22
00:01:24.881 --> 00:01:28.203
Mr. Dunn showed the campers how to wring the water out of the shirts.

23
00:01:30.332 --> 00:01:34.055
"Now we're ready to make our designs," he said.

24
00:01:34.075 --> 00:01:37.318
"Can anyone guess how I made mine?"

25
00:01:38.319 --> 00:01:39.660
Izzie studied his shirt.

26
00:01:42.162 --> 00:01:44.504
She also saw rubber bands on the table.

27
00:01:44.524 --> 00:01:50.068
"You put rubber bands around the T-shirt before you dyed it!"

28
00:01:50.409 --> 00:01:51.049
Izzie said.

29
00:01:51.069 --> 00:01:53.992
"The dye couldn't get under the rubber bands.

30
00:01:54.772 --> 00:01:56.774
That's why there are those white stripes!"

31
00:01:57.935 --> 00:01:59.176
Mr. Dunn smiled.

32
00:01:59.808 --> 00:02:00.869
"Good thinking, Izzie."

33
00:02:00.889 --> 00:02:05.590
"First twist your shirt," the teacher said.

34
00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:09.412
"Then make sections with rubber bands.

35
00:02:10.572 --> 00:02:12.993
Each rubber band will become a white stripe.

36
00:02:15.675 --> 00:02:19.816
To make a pattern of circles, twist the middle section of the shirt.

37
00:02:20.937 --> 00:02:23.558
Add rubber bands to make rings around your circle."

38
00:02:23.578 --> 00:02:27.239
"I want stripes, just like yours, Mr.

39
00:02:27.299 --> 00:02:28.720
Dunn," Izzie said.

40
00:02:29.796 --> 00:02:32.277
"I'm making circles," said Nina.

41
00:02:33.298 --> 00:02:34.998
The boys chose circles too.

42
00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.761
"Now it's time to dye.

43
00:02:42.802 --> 00:02:46.043
Carefully squeeze dye onto each section."

44
00:02:46.323 --> 00:02:47.864
Mr. Dunn demonstrated.

45
00:02:52.206 --> 00:02:56.268
can use just two colors, or as many as you want," Mr.

46
00:02:56.328 --> 00:02:56.948
Dunn said.

47
00:02:58.024 --> 00:02:59.004
Izzie looked at Mr.

48
00:02:59.044 --> 00:02:59.745
Dunn's shirt.

49
00:03:00.805 --> 00:03:04.226
It had green stripes at the top and blue ones at the bottom.

50
00:03:05.126 --> 00:03:06.946
Izzie used those colors too.

51
00:03:06.966 --> 00:03:10.667
"Now put the shirts in plastic bags.

52
00:03:11.828 --> 00:03:15.849
The dye needs to soak in for the rest of the day," said Mr.

53
00:03:15.889 --> 00:03:20.930
Dunn. "At home you'll have to hang up the shirts to let them dry."

54
00:03:22.311 --> 00:03:24.571
The kids set their bagged shirts aside.

55
00:03:25.531 --> 00:03:27.112
But Izzie wasn't good at waiting.

56
00:03:28.188 --> 00:03:30.250
She wanted to see her shirt now.

57
00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:33.492
"Can we peek at the shirts, to check our designs?"

58
00:03:33.992 --> 00:03:34.593
she asked.

59
00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:36.974
"No." Mr.

60
00:03:37.034 --> 00:03:38.015
Dunn shook his head.

61
00:03:38.035 --> 00:03:40.236
"You have to wait, Izzie."

62
00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.862
is so hard," Izzie thought.

63
00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.463
What if she had made a mistake?

64
00:03:51.704 --> 00:03:53.806
What if her shirt didn't come out like Mr.

65
00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:58.152
Dunn's? Finally the teacher announced, "It's time!"

66
00:03:59.293 --> 00:04:01.054
The kids rushed back to their shirts.

67
00:04:05.656 --> 00:04:08.077
Izzie thought the other campers' shirts looked great.

68
00:04:09.197 --> 00:04:10.898
Then she took hers out of the bag.

69
00:04:14.179 --> 00:04:14.880
She gasped.

70
00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:18.821
There were only two green stripes and five blue ones.

71
00:04:18.841 --> 00:04:23.443
"Mr. Dunn, it doesn't look like your shirt at all!"

72
00:04:23.844 --> 00:04:24.444
she cried.

73
00:04:29.228 --> 00:04:31.711
"It's much better than my shirt," Mr.

74
00:04:31.751 --> 00:04:32.371
Dunn said.

75
00:04:32.391 --> 00:04:35.855
"The uneven pattern is beautiful!

76
00:04:37.016 --> 00:04:40.619
You'll see how great it looks when we all wear our shirts on Friday."

77
00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:42.781
Izzie smiled.

78
00:04:43.322 --> 00:04:45.284
Now she couldn't wait until Friday!
